        "original_id": "6244e155-6ed8-5f3b-9698-f7821af7112f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Manhattan West, Lower Manhattan, Financial District, New York City, Liberty Street, Broadway\n- Buildings: Manhattan West west tower, Singer Building, Singer Tower\n- Companies: Singer Manufacturing Company\n- Topics: skyscraper height, building completion, headquarters\n\nFacts:\n- The Singer Building, also called Singer Tower, was a 47-story office building at Liberty Street and Broadway in Lower Manhattan's Financial District in New York.\n- The Singer Building was completed in 1908 as the headquarters of the Singer Manufacturing Company.\n- Upon completion, the taller west tower at Manhattan West will rise 995 feet to its roof.\n- Upon completion, the taller west tower at Manhattan West will be one of the tallest buildings in New York City and the world.",
